# Native dependencies must not be compiled from source. There is no compiler on
# the Windows CI runner or the reference machine, by design: the stack premise is
# Node-API prebuilds, not a toolchain.
#
# better-sqlite3 13 ships an ABI-independent Node-API prebuild per arch (it loads
# and runs on Node 26 with no build), but it carries a binding.gyp and sets
# gypfile:false to tell npm not to build it. npm 11 ignores gypfile:false and runs
# node-gyp rebuild anyway, which fails without Visual Studio. npm has no
# per-package way to suppress that one build, and the older prebuild-install line
# (<=12) has no Node-26 prebuild and fails worse. So install scripts are disabled
# globally here. This is a last resort, chosen only after the narrow and the
# version fixes were shown not to exist on Node 26.
#
# The cost, stated because it is real: every dependency's install and postinstall
# script is skipped, present and future. That is the fail-silent pattern this
# project distrusts, so it is contained: better-sqlite3 loads from its bundled
# prebuild without its install script (no compiler needed), and
# src/build/install-scripts.test.ts fails if any dependency gains an install
# script not in its allowlist, so a future native dep cannot silently go
# unbuilt: adding it is a deliberate, reviewed act.
ignore-scripts=true
